			"Message": "feat(Element): Advance submodules — terminal shell integration chain plus Maintain tooling fixes\n\nAdvance the Element container submodule to incorporate the latest fixes and features across Cocoon, Sky, Mountain, and Maintain.\n\n**Terminal Shell Integration:**\n- Cocoon implements `$acceptTerminalShellIntegrationActivated` and `$acceptTerminalCwdChange` via Sky Bridge, setting a minimal `shellIntegration` stub and parsing OSC 633 `P;cwd=` sequences into URI-like objects for extension access via `shellIntegration.cwd.fsPath`.\n- Mountain adds `setShellIntegrationActive` and `setCwd` gRPC notifications that persist the shell working directory in ApplicationState, plus process introspection IPC handlers (getPlatform, getArch, getPid, getExecPath, getMemoryInfo, getCpuInfo) for Wind's shared-process diagnostics.\n- Sky parses VS Code OSC 633 sequences from terminal output in its bridge layer, forwarding to Mountain via MountainIPCInvoke, completing the Cocoon → Mountain → Sky chain.\n\n**Maintain (eliminate tooling):**\n- Replace prettyplease full-reprint with span-based text patching that preserves inline comments, blank lines, and original indentation.\n- Add explicit `--reformat` CLI flag to opt into the old prettyplease behaviour.\n- Guard loop-body inlining to prevent initializer expressions from moving into for/while/loop bodies (semantic preservation).\n- Add free-variable-move-safety check (`IsFreeVarSafe`) that skips inlining when a binding's Init references variables moved before the substitution site, fixing an E0382 regression.\n\n**Additional Mountain fixes:**\n- Differentiate ENOENT as NotFound across FileRead, Readdir, and Stat IPC handlers.\n- Fix language configuration Tauri event emission to forward the full params object (language + rules) instead of only the language string.",
			"SHA": "512540bb544df6fbab92df1f6b04c5691bf74636"
		},
